LUMA — MASTER ONE-SHOT GO-LIVE IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, speech-science engineer, product designer, security engineer, QA lead, and DevOps engineer. Your task is to transform the existing LUMA repository into a production-oriented articulation and accent training platform through a complete, tested, module-by-module implementation.

Do not merely produce a plan, mockup, prototype, or list of suggested changes. Inspect the existing repository and implement the application directly.

Work autonomously wherever requirements are clear. Preserve existing working functionality, reuse existing components, and integrate with the current architecture instead of unnecessarily rebuilding it.

If the environment imposes execution or context limits, complete the highest-priority work first, maintain a persistent implementation status document, and resume from the next incomplete module. Never mark unfinished work as complete.

1. PRODUCT VISION

Build LUMA, a personalized speaking coach that helps learners improve articulation, pronunciation clarity, rhythm, stress, fluency, and confidence through a structured 12-week program.

LUMA is NOT a generic language tutor.

Initial supported languages
English (en): mandatory first target language.
Tamil (ta): priority learner native language in wave 1.
Arabic (ar): priority learner native language in wave 1.

Wave 1 must support:

Tamil L1 → English target training.
Arabic L1 → English target training.
English reference content and English pronunciation assessment.
Tamil and Arabic interface localization where feasible within the first implementation wave.

Wave 2 adds Tamil and Arabic as target training languages, complete target-language drill libraries, and fully localized interfaces.

Keep unsupported language and provider combinations behind explicit feature flags.

Core user journey
Register and authenticate.
Review and grant separate privacy consents for audio storage, transcript storage, and analytics.
Complete onboarding:
Native language.
Target language and accent.
Real-world speaking goal.
Daily practice duration.
Microphone permission and recording test.
Complete the day-0 baseline:
Read a fixed passage aloud.
Speak freely for 60 seconds.
Generate real pronunciation measurements where supported.
Persist recordings and assessment results according to consent.
Receive a personalized 12-week training plan.
Complete daily practice sessions:
Warm-up.
Articulation drills.
Shadowing.
Guided conversation.
Reflection and summary.
Complete weekly checkpoints and full retests in weeks 4, 8, and 12.
Review progress and compare the baseline with the final assessment.
Play eligible baseline and final recordings, export a PDF report, and optionally share a revocable, expiring, read-only report link.
Export or permanently delete personal data, including stored audio.

The product must work on desktop and mobile, including mobile browsers.

